  "body": "The spec says\r\n\r\n```\r\nhr {\r\n  color: gray;\r\n  border-style: inset;\r\n  border-width: 1px;\r\n  margin-block-start: 0.5em;\r\n  margin-inline-end: auto;\r\n  margin-block-end: 0.5em;\r\n  margin-inline-start: auto;\r\n}\r\n```\r\nPer test results in https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/pull/6115 only Gecko has the `color: gray` rule; other browsers don't have that.\r\n\r\nChecking http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/5221 it seems WebKit/Chromium/EdgeHTML also don't have default styles for `border-color`, but just render some light-gray color if author CSS hasn't specified a `border-color`.\r\n\r\nGecko also has a darker default rendering (following from the color `gray`) of the borders compared to the other browsers.\r\n\r\nWhat do we want to do here?",
